1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Bastard!

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:13,000
Lieutenant Marito!

3
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:19,000
All units spread out!

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:21,000
Didn't work.

5
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:23,000
I thought that if it was going to be using lightning,

6
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:26,000
it might have been an opening for us while it was switching over.

7
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:29,000
I don't think it's going to be that easy for us.

8
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:32,000
That being the case, what are the options?

9
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:34,000
Lieutenant Marito!

10
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Message from the Deutalian.

11
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:38,000
HQ has ordered us to pull out.

12
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Pull out? Wait, everyone?

13
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:44,000
Dale's Platoon and Orlov's Platoon should have gotten the order by now, too.

14
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:45,000
But...

15
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:46,000
But what?

16
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Retreat! Retreat!

17
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:53,000
No, Dale's 2-2!

18
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Where is he? Where's the enemy?

19
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:58,000
Commander!

20
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:02,000
That invisible cataphrac we didn't take down is over there!

21
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:03,000
Crap!

22
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:06,000
Clydesdale leader to Orlov leader!

23
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:07,000
Do you read me?

24
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Retreat!

25
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:11,000
This is Orlov leader.

26
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:12,000
It's too late.

27
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:14,000
I'm the only one...

28
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:18,000
Left over here!

29
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:23,000
Lightning...

30
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:24,000
invisibility...

31
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:26,000
There must be...

32
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:27,000
another one.

33
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,000
Their orders are to continue...

34
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:33,000
encircle...

35
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:34,000
and then eliminate.

36
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:36,000
By your command, my lord.

37
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:37,000
My lord.

38
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:47,000
Princess of Salem!

39
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:49,000
What's this?

40
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:51,000
I've done all I could.

41
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:56,000
It was the best I could do.

42
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:01,000
I'm sorry...

43
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:02,000
Slain.

44
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:09,000
This cannot be...

45
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:10,000
This cannot be...

46
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:11,000
This cannot be...

47
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:12,000
you.

48
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:27,100
No!

49
00:02:42,000 --> 00:03:11,980
Thank you.

50
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:41,980
Thank you.

51
00:03:42,000 --> 00:04:11,980
Thank you.

52
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:14,760
Now, young Kai's come!

53
00:04:22,520 --> 00:04:24,000
Now you can all move out.

54
00:04:24,380 --> 00:04:27,180
That cloud of smoke will hamper the enemy's vision for the time being.

55
00:04:27,660 --> 00:04:28,120
Go!

56
00:04:29,060 --> 00:04:29,580
Roger!

57
00:04:29,580 --> 00:04:36,740
Also, this smoke will help us so we can attack.

58
00:04:41,480 --> 00:04:42,360
I've got him.

59
00:04:42,520 --> 00:04:43,520
To your right, look out!

60
00:04:43,520 --> 00:04:52,560
Mustang leader!

61
00:04:52,880 --> 00:04:54,040
What's going on, Kaizuka?

62
00:04:54,280 --> 00:04:56,340
I thought your job was to keep lightning elsewhere.

63
00:04:56,700 --> 00:04:57,360
Sorry, lieutenant.

64
00:04:57,780 --> 00:04:59,680
Suddenly, its focus just completely shifted.

65
00:05:00,080 --> 00:05:01,440
As if it knew where you were.

66
00:05:02,440 --> 00:05:02,960
Crap!

67
00:05:02,960 --> 00:05:08,840
Are we surrounded?

68
00:05:09,580 --> 00:05:10,680
Looks that way.

69
00:05:10,680 --> 00:05:23,900
The Deucalion!

70
00:05:23,900 --> 00:05:24,040
The Deucalion!

71
00:05:31,220 --> 00:05:32,060
Damage report.

72
00:05:32,200 --> 00:05:32,900
We're okay, ma'am.

73
00:05:33,140 --> 00:05:34,200
The charge dissipated.

74
00:05:34,600 --> 00:05:35,360
Set us down.

75
00:05:35,620 --> 00:05:37,120
We're extracting our cataphracts.

76
00:05:37,260 --> 00:05:38,060
Right here, ma'am?

77
00:05:38,520 --> 00:05:39,660
We're in the middle of the enemy.

78
00:05:39,980 --> 00:05:40,920
Just land us.

79
00:05:42,760 --> 00:05:44,360
Our airspeed is not optimal.

80
00:05:44,700 --> 00:05:45,420
There's a tailwind.

81
00:05:45,480 --> 00:05:46,640
You're descending too fast.

82
00:05:46,820 --> 00:05:47,360
We're okay.

83
00:05:47,720 --> 00:05:49,040
The Alt-Noah Drive can take it.

84
00:05:49,420 --> 00:05:50,740
Anti-grad device to maximum.

85
00:05:50,740 --> 00:05:53,560
365 meters per second descent rate.

86
00:05:56,680 --> 00:05:58,000
You get aboard.

87
00:05:58,460 --> 00:05:59,700
The Gaiden deals, platoon.

88
00:06:00,160 --> 00:06:00,760
Now hurry!

89
00:06:02,160 --> 00:06:03,700
Open the ventral hatch.

90
00:06:03,980 --> 00:06:05,360
Get those cataphracts inside.

91
00:06:05,820 --> 00:06:06,860
Enemy closing in.

92
00:06:08,400 --> 00:06:09,320
Hostile cataphracts.

93
00:06:09,440 --> 00:06:10,640
Inbound at or nine o'clock.

94
00:06:12,200 --> 00:06:13,480
Main guns, fire.

95
00:06:18,260 --> 00:06:20,240
Cataphract retrieval complete, Captain.

96
00:06:20,740 --> 00:06:21,420
Let's go.

97
00:06:25,820 --> 00:06:26,900
What is that?

98
00:06:27,560 --> 00:06:29,320
Another enemy cataphract, Aft.

99
00:06:29,560 --> 00:06:31,340
Same type as the one we just destroyed.

100
00:06:32,020 --> 00:06:32,580
Reinforcements?

101
00:06:32,720 --> 00:06:33,800
Now there's another one.

102
00:06:34,280 --> 00:06:35,640
They are not support troops.

103
00:06:36,080 --> 00:06:36,740
I think they're...

104
00:06:50,740 --> 00:06:52,040
Radar returns.

105
00:06:52,600 --> 00:06:53,260
There's 12.

106
00:06:53,680 --> 00:06:54,160
24.

107
00:06:54,940 --> 00:06:55,820
Numbers increasing.

108
00:06:55,820 --> 00:06:57,900
Duplication ability?

109
00:06:58,220 --> 00:06:59,520
All engines ahead, both!

110
00:06:59,700 --> 00:07:00,260
Damn it!

111
00:07:00,260 --> 00:07:15,700
Wither radar, doubler radar, both are offline.

112
00:07:16,020 --> 00:07:16,760
Not good.

113
00:07:16,760 --> 00:07:19,860
Invisible Zero must have messed up our entire electrical system.

114
00:07:20,100 --> 00:07:21,000
Radio's out too.

115
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:23,180
GPS displays on the fritz.

116
00:07:23,180 --> 00:07:24,880
And 2D radar is offline.

117
00:07:25,200 --> 00:07:26,120
What do we do?

118
00:07:26,420 --> 00:07:27,160
Keep it together.

119
00:07:27,960 --> 00:07:28,860
Continue the ascent.

120
00:07:29,540 --> 00:07:30,220
Aye, aye, ma'am.

121
00:07:30,220 --> 00:07:33,740
So we are both clear.

122
00:07:33,960 --> 00:07:36,560
Are you willing to swear your loyalty to Count Troyard?

123
00:07:37,080 --> 00:07:37,560
Yes.

124
00:07:38,080 --> 00:07:39,940
Then I shall immediately inform him.

125
00:07:40,540 --> 00:07:42,580
There is a favor I would like to ask of you.

126
00:07:42,780 --> 00:07:43,680
Yes, what is it?

127
00:07:43,680 --> 00:07:47,040
Is an audience with Princesses Salem a possibility?

128
00:07:47,540 --> 00:07:49,600
You wish to see her highness?

129
00:07:50,120 --> 00:07:50,500
Yes.

130
00:07:50,900 --> 00:07:52,740
And if possible, with Count Troyard.

131
00:07:53,640 --> 00:07:55,740
That is no small request, my lord.

132
00:07:56,220 --> 00:07:58,680
I will endeavor to see that you are accommodated.

133
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:03,200
However, a task of this nature does come at a price.

134
00:08:03,600 --> 00:08:04,560
Understood, my lord.

135
00:08:04,940 --> 00:08:09,300
I must say, after difficulties such as yours, another man might have lost his way.

136
00:08:09,300 --> 00:08:15,760
Being seen well by the Count, in addition to Princesses of Salem, would be most beneficial.

137
00:08:16,700 --> 00:08:19,520
However, do not wear ambition on your sleeve.

138
00:08:20,040 --> 00:08:22,100
There is a chance it could cause you to stumble.

139
00:08:24,540 --> 00:08:25,460
We're saying.

140
00:08:30,020 --> 00:08:32,480
That is not the real Princesses of Salem.

141
00:08:35,600 --> 00:08:37,020
I'm going into space.

142
00:08:37,500 --> 00:08:38,140
Prepare a shuttle.

143
00:08:39,300 --> 00:08:42,260
Congratulations on your victory, my lord slain.

144
00:08:42,900 --> 00:08:44,300
No cause for celebration.

145
00:08:44,700 --> 00:08:46,280
Not when the enemy escaped us.

146
00:08:47,300 --> 00:08:49,740
You did achieve the objective of securing territory.

147
00:08:50,520 --> 00:08:52,060
Is that not sufficient success?

148
00:08:52,640 --> 00:08:55,460
This will certainly cause more knights to swear loyalty.

149
00:08:56,060 --> 00:08:57,460
We must not be complacent.

150
00:08:58,560 --> 00:09:02,620
There are very few things less reliable than a knight's loyalty.

151
00:09:03,580 --> 00:09:04,960
We know that well, my lord.

152
00:09:05,560 --> 00:09:06,300
Now, my lord.

153
00:09:06,720 --> 00:09:09,060
Concerning that request from Count Borocruz.

154
00:09:09,060 --> 00:09:10,600
How shall I reply to him?

155
00:09:10,600 --> 00:09:10,620
How shall I reply to him?

156
00:09:10,620 --> 00:09:12,500
Very well, my lord.

157
00:09:12,500 --> 00:09:14,680
Mazurak, was that his name?

158
00:09:15,460 --> 00:09:17,860
If he wishes to see the princess, we will let him.

159
00:09:18,400 --> 00:09:22,720
She seems to be quite happy with her role of further extending our base of power.

160
00:09:23,420 --> 00:09:25,740
At least, for the time being.

161
00:09:25,740 --> 00:09:35,860
This is bad.

162
00:09:35,860 --> 00:09:38,580
And it's way past any quick and easy patch.

163
00:09:38,780 --> 00:09:39,740
I hate this.

164
00:09:40,160 --> 00:09:41,580
Night vision's out of whack also.

165
00:09:41,920 --> 00:09:44,120
So I don't even dare to try to fly by eye.

166
00:09:45,860 --> 00:09:46,760
Where's the problem?

167
00:09:47,280 --> 00:09:48,500
Is it in the sensor system?

168
00:09:48,700 --> 00:09:50,120
That's very good, Ensign Kaisuka.

169
00:09:50,300 --> 00:09:51,160
How did you know that?

170
00:09:51,160 --> 00:09:52,480
The signs are there.

171
00:09:52,820 --> 00:09:55,560
It's faint, but the fuselage is still holding a charge.

172
00:09:56,320 --> 00:09:59,280
A malfunction with the engine isn't very likely with this vessel.

173
00:09:59,620 --> 00:10:00,600
In which case...

174
00:10:00,600 --> 00:10:02,360
Well, can you do anything about it?

175
00:10:02,440 --> 00:10:03,720
We can't fly like this.

176
00:10:03,720 --> 00:10:13,840
Well, you might want to try dropping a little lower.

177
00:10:14,360 --> 00:10:16,260
Just enough to get us below enemy radar.

178
00:10:16,580 --> 00:10:21,240
But now that I can't use the GPWS or the altimeter, I'm scared of approaching the ground.

179
00:10:21,360 --> 00:10:22,480
There's no reason to worry.

180
00:10:22,940 --> 00:10:23,840
We're at 9,200.

181
00:10:24,680 --> 00:10:26,820
You can really measure that just by looking?

182
00:10:28,380 --> 00:10:30,300
Can you also get VOR stations?

183
00:10:31,040 --> 00:10:31,420
Yes.

184
00:10:31,420 --> 00:10:34,600
Once you have both signals, let me know, okay?

185
00:10:34,860 --> 00:10:36,140
Then I'll calculate our radial.

186
00:10:36,460 --> 00:10:36,780
Sure.

187
00:10:37,180 --> 00:10:37,840
What's our heading?

188
00:10:38,240 --> 00:10:39,820
I was trying to put us on 110.

189
00:10:40,440 --> 00:10:41,820
And you're almost there now.

190
00:10:42,440 --> 00:10:43,620
Maintain a vector offset.

191
00:10:44,140 --> 00:10:45,420
Three degrees for two minutes.

192
00:10:46,920 --> 00:10:48,060
This is not good.

193
00:10:48,440 --> 00:10:50,300
Are we caught in some kind of nasty turbulence?

194
00:10:50,800 --> 00:10:52,060
This goes on a while.

195
00:10:52,480 --> 00:10:53,660
Let's adjust our speed.

196
00:10:53,920 --> 00:10:54,880
No, I've got it.

197
00:10:56,700 --> 00:10:58,240
I think I can handle this.

198
00:10:58,240 --> 00:10:59,080
Like earlier.

199
00:10:59,940 --> 00:11:00,480
I see that.

200
00:11:00,480 --> 00:11:03,860
Well, I guess experience is really what's needed here now.

201
00:11:04,260 --> 00:11:06,260
I'll let you know when I pick up an LLZ.

202
00:11:06,720 --> 00:11:07,160
Thanks.

203
00:11:09,860 --> 00:11:10,840
Thank you for that.

204
00:11:11,440 --> 00:11:13,680
Maybe we should be the ones who are thanking you.

205
00:11:14,120 --> 00:11:18,280
Though Lieutenant Marito said he was just shocked that you would do something so crazy.

206
00:11:18,280 --> 00:11:20,560
I do not want to hear that from you.

207
00:11:21,660 --> 00:11:23,400
Tell him that was my reply.

208
00:11:24,840 --> 00:11:26,200
That is good to hear.

209
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:30,320
So then, preparations for the founding are all proceeding smoothly?

210
00:11:30,780 --> 00:11:31,200
Yes.

211
00:11:31,340 --> 00:11:34,660
I can barely stand this awful wait for this new kingdom's birth.

212
00:11:35,060 --> 00:11:37,240
And then to see your home world at long last.

213
00:11:37,240 --> 00:11:39,880
Merely a world inhabited by vulgar trash.

214
00:11:40,380 --> 00:11:43,160
Hardly the restful image conjured up by the word home.

215
00:11:43,680 --> 00:11:47,860
Actually, I never really had a place that felt like home.

216
00:11:47,860 --> 00:11:50,900
And actually, neither did I.

217
00:11:52,180 --> 00:11:54,980
Not on verse, nor in royal eminence.

218
00:11:55,700 --> 00:11:58,440
Has there ever been a way for me to find solace?

219
00:11:58,440 --> 00:12:07,060
But now, Slane, anywhere that I can be with you, in any circumstance, that is my home.

220
00:12:10,300 --> 00:12:11,640
You honor me.

221
00:12:15,280 --> 00:12:17,620
I shall call on you again later.

222
00:12:18,280 --> 00:12:21,560
But Slane, can't you stay a little longer?

223
00:12:24,400 --> 00:12:25,760
So sorry, Highness.

224
00:12:26,220 --> 00:12:27,900
But matters require my attention.

225
00:12:28,440 --> 00:12:29,460
Please forgive me.

226
00:12:29,460 --> 00:12:29,540
Please forgive me.

227
00:12:45,540 --> 00:12:46,100
Inaho!

228
00:12:50,720 --> 00:12:51,980
Oh, Inka.

229
00:12:52,800 --> 00:12:53,840
What's going on?

230
00:12:55,260 --> 00:12:58,420
Yesterday, Nina was going on about you being on the bridge.

231
00:12:58,440 --> 00:12:59,860
And helping them out up there.

232
00:13:00,220 --> 00:13:00,720
Oh, yeah.

233
00:13:00,940 --> 00:13:01,300
Right.

234
00:13:01,640 --> 00:13:02,800
Uh, Inaho?

235
00:13:03,740 --> 00:13:05,000
Is there something wrong?

236
00:13:05,660 --> 00:13:06,300
Like what?

237
00:13:06,540 --> 00:13:07,780
Come on, what do you mean what?

238
00:13:10,940 --> 00:13:12,440
Maybe it's nothing, but...

239
00:13:12,440 --> 00:13:16,140
What do you think about the enemy coordinating their attack like that?

240
00:13:16,140 --> 00:13:20,420
Maybe it's been so hard they're forced to swallow their pride and work together.

241
00:13:21,380 --> 00:13:24,860
Judging by the outcome, I don't think we have that much to fear from it.

242
00:13:24,860 --> 00:13:28,780
Well, then, do you suppose it's connected to that proclamation?

243
00:13:29,780 --> 00:13:33,360
That orbital knight slain Troyard is the one behind Princess of Salem.

244
00:13:34,140 --> 00:13:36,500
Even young Kaisuke seems to think he's something special.

245
00:13:36,500 --> 00:13:45,620
If this opponent is setting things into motion with a specific goal in mind, it's certainly not some simple scheme we can counter with superior resources.

246
00:13:46,900 --> 00:13:47,620
Enter.

247
00:13:47,620 --> 00:13:52,600
PFC Matsuribi with a message.

248
00:13:55,020 --> 00:13:56,460
Dispatch from HQ, ma'am.

249
00:13:58,880 --> 00:14:00,860
A request for reinforcements?

250
00:14:01,580 --> 00:14:04,400
Launch all-out attack on newly captured territory.

251
00:14:04,940 --> 00:14:05,880
Take it back.

252
00:14:05,880 --> 00:14:08,580
So they can use us as bait?

253
00:14:12,480 --> 00:14:14,000
That's what it sounds like.

254
00:14:15,480 --> 00:14:17,580
And how have you been feeling since then?

255
00:14:18,420 --> 00:14:21,180
Well, physically, just fine.

256
00:14:22,300 --> 00:14:27,040
As to my memory, however, it is a little hazy, I have to admit.

257
00:14:27,620 --> 00:14:28,680
Hardly surprising.

258
00:14:29,180 --> 00:14:32,640
The fact that you came back to consciousness, that was a miracle.

259
00:14:32,640 --> 00:14:40,000
Perhaps, you should not try to force yourself to remember.

260
00:14:41,560 --> 00:14:43,520
Thank you, Slain, very much.

261
00:14:45,160 --> 00:14:47,300
I fear I must take my leave now.

262
00:14:47,980 --> 00:14:49,340
Try to get some rest, please.

263
00:14:49,580 --> 00:14:50,040
Yes.

264
00:14:50,400 --> 00:14:52,440
Look after Her Highness until I return.

265
00:14:53,780 --> 00:14:56,160
Milord, do you have a moment?

266
00:14:56,160 --> 00:15:02,820
I believe I know what you wish to ask.

267
00:15:03,340 --> 00:15:04,600
The proclamation, yes?

268
00:15:05,720 --> 00:15:08,680
Taking me as her husband, founding a new kingdom.

269
00:15:10,200 --> 00:15:13,000
That proclamation issued by Princess Lemrina

270
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:16,680
was simply a direct result of the weakness in my heart.

271
00:15:17,240 --> 00:15:19,320
Princess Asalem is going to wake up.

272
00:15:19,320 --> 00:15:23,220
I tried to hold on to that belief, but was unable to in the end.

273
00:15:24,060 --> 00:15:27,000
I had given up, deep inside somewhere.

274
00:15:30,320 --> 00:15:33,340
It was then that the miracle came to pass,

275
00:15:33,380 --> 00:15:35,700
as if to reprimand me for being such a fool.

276
00:15:36,400 --> 00:15:38,660
Now, of course, things are completely different.

277
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:43,300
And so my focus, therefore, must now be on how best to keep Her Highness happy.

278
00:15:43,700 --> 00:15:45,560
Only that, and nothing else.

279
00:15:45,560 --> 00:15:50,520
But my lord, what of Princess Lemrina?

280
00:15:51,020 --> 00:15:53,380
As to what she hopes the future will hold,

281
00:15:53,700 --> 00:15:55,020
I believe I have an idea.

282
00:15:55,680 --> 00:15:58,420
I think that she wishes the same thing I do.

283
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:01,020
A place where she can find some solace.

284
00:16:02,180 --> 00:16:06,360
But I fear that to be something that we would never be able to achieve together.

285
00:16:07,120 --> 00:16:09,860
So now may not be the time to tell her everything.

286
00:16:10,540 --> 00:16:12,760
And even if she looks down on me,

287
00:16:12,800 --> 00:16:15,340
or if she has no respect for what I'm doing here,

288
00:16:15,560 --> 00:16:18,720
it doesn't mean anything to me anyway.

289
00:16:21,420 --> 00:16:22,940
It is so ironic.

290
00:16:24,200 --> 00:16:27,620
I had waited so desperately for Her Highness to awaken.

291
00:16:27,620 --> 00:16:33,320
But now I, I hope that her memory never returns.

292
00:16:33,320 --> 00:16:43,020
My lord, your willingness and resolve to serve my trusted Count Troyard fills me with such joy that I cannot contain it.

293
00:16:43,580 --> 00:16:45,440
Your Highness is extremely gracious.

294
00:16:46,380 --> 00:16:51,880
I am determined and fully prepared to serve both your Highness and Count Troyard with wholehearted devotion.

295
00:16:51,880 --> 00:16:57,260
I, too, was deeply moved by Count Mazurak's unwavering allegiance and personal strength,

296
00:16:57,740 --> 00:17:01,500
as he swore to escape and rise up once again in the name of verse,

297
00:17:01,940 --> 00:17:03,780
even as he was being held prisoner.

298
00:17:03,780 --> 00:17:05,220
Begging your pardon, Highness.

299
00:17:05,220 --> 00:17:11,220
I am given to understand that you yourself were subjected to similar hardships during your stay on Earth.

300
00:17:11,220 --> 00:17:19,420
Yes, the situation was similar, and the Terrans are all vulgar trash in so many ways.

301
00:17:19,420 --> 00:17:24,540
There was not even a single one where your Highness might have grown close?

302
00:17:24,740 --> 00:17:26,380
I would never do such a thing.

303
00:17:27,220 --> 00:17:30,820
My handmaiden had the task of interacting with them if necessary.

304
00:17:32,240 --> 00:17:37,260
There once was a time when I entertained the notion of reconciling with those people.

305
00:17:37,960 --> 00:17:40,580
A foolish idea, quickly discarded.

306
00:17:40,580 --> 00:17:47,140
Why is Slain not here to help at a time like this?

307
00:17:47,660 --> 00:17:48,620
Pardon, Your Highness.

308
00:17:49,240 --> 00:17:52,260
Lord Slain has many preparations to oversee for the war.

309
00:17:52,580 --> 00:17:54,140
He said as much to me earlier.

310
00:17:54,540 --> 00:17:58,220
He is too absent, locking himself away in his castle too much.

311
00:17:58,380 --> 00:18:00,360
Whatever he's doing, can he not do it here?

312
00:18:00,780 --> 00:18:03,220
I am told that it is due to precious resources.

313
00:18:04,400 --> 00:18:06,740
Well then, I shall go to him.

314
00:18:06,880 --> 00:18:07,660
Please, Your Highness.

315
00:18:08,320 --> 00:18:09,140
Yes, that's it.

316
00:18:09,140 --> 00:18:11,120
I'll go to his landing castle.

317
00:18:11,900 --> 00:18:12,940
No, Your Highness.

318
00:18:16,820 --> 00:18:18,100
Are you injured, Highness?

319
00:18:18,300 --> 00:18:18,820
Are you hurt?

320
00:18:19,200 --> 00:18:20,120
A thousand pardons.

321
00:18:20,320 --> 00:18:23,960
Just how long will it be?

322
00:18:27,020 --> 00:18:29,540
Please, how long will it be?

323
00:18:34,480 --> 00:18:36,960
Let me see you to your room, Highness.

324
00:18:39,140 --> 00:19:00,440
Please, pardon the delay.

325
00:19:00,440 --> 00:19:04,740
My Lord Count Mazurek, would you please follow me to the parlor?

326
00:19:05,160 --> 00:19:08,120
Now that my credentials have been thoroughly checked...

327
00:19:08,120 --> 00:19:09,240
My deep apologies.

328
00:19:09,720 --> 00:19:10,720
Oh, not at all.

329
00:19:11,120 --> 00:19:12,340
The blunder here is mine.

330
00:19:12,780 --> 00:19:14,720
To think I allowed my ship to break down.

331
00:19:15,720 --> 00:19:17,840
How fortunate for me I was in your vicinity.

332
00:19:17,840 --> 00:19:25,100
So I guess that Count Troyard is still working over at the moon base?

333
00:19:25,700 --> 00:19:26,140
Yes.

334
00:19:26,360 --> 00:19:27,940
I regret you cannot see him.

335
00:19:28,200 --> 00:19:30,960
But Lord Harklight is on his way and ought to be here soon.

336
00:19:30,960 --> 00:19:36,280
I made certain they were gone before I did this.

337
00:19:38,020 --> 00:19:41,720
Troyard is coming back here from the moon base a lot more than is really necessary.

338
00:19:43,760 --> 00:19:46,360
Meaning that Princess of Salem must be.

339
00:19:46,360 --> 00:19:57,320
My Lord, if you would please wait here.

340
00:19:57,960 --> 00:19:58,160
Hmm?

341
00:19:59,160 --> 00:20:00,920
Are those Terran flowers?

342
00:20:02,180 --> 00:20:02,780
Yes.

343
00:20:03,320 --> 00:20:06,840
It's obvious this castle has undergone quite the transformation.

344
00:20:07,320 --> 00:20:08,700
You can see that, my Lord?

345
00:20:08,700 --> 00:20:11,300
I was acquainted with its former master.

346
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:15,700
He detested all things Terran, fearing that they might be harboring microorganisms.

347
00:20:16,600 --> 00:20:18,720
Oh, certainly there is no such problem.

348
00:20:19,140 --> 00:20:20,460
Terran flowers are safe.

349
00:20:21,420 --> 00:20:23,260
Oh, so then you have been down there.

350
00:20:23,840 --> 00:20:26,420
No, just repeating what I have been told.

351
00:20:26,780 --> 00:20:30,700
I had heard Princess of Salem had a personal attendant, but I did not expect...

352
00:20:31,300 --> 00:20:32,540
Is it you?

353
00:20:32,880 --> 00:20:34,060
No, I'm not.

354
00:20:34,180 --> 00:20:37,260
I mean, when Her Highness went to Earth, she was all alone.

355
00:20:37,260 --> 00:20:38,600
I'm so sorry.

356
00:20:38,920 --> 00:20:40,660
We were not speaking of Earth, were we?

357
00:20:42,220 --> 00:20:43,860
Please, I must be going.

358
00:20:46,020 --> 00:20:48,300
You can honestly say you have not been there.

359
00:20:48,800 --> 00:20:50,620
That you truly do not know what happened?

360
00:20:51,740 --> 00:20:54,000
What about a boy named Inaho Kaisuka?

361
00:20:59,240 --> 00:21:00,700
How long will it be?

362
00:21:02,540 --> 00:21:03,700
Tell me, sister.

363
00:21:05,060 --> 00:21:06,360
How long will it take?

364
00:21:07,260 --> 00:21:10,380
For you to release your grip on his feelings.

365
00:21:11,340 --> 00:21:12,220
How long?

366
00:21:13,540 --> 00:21:14,700
He brought this for me?

367
00:21:14,840 --> 00:21:15,660
Yes, m'lady.

368
00:21:16,220 --> 00:21:19,240
He said he wished it to be presented to you in particular.

369
00:21:20,100 --> 00:21:23,020
To the princess who knew about Earth is what he said.

370
00:21:23,260 --> 00:21:24,260
Ah.

371
00:21:25,260 --> 00:21:26,260
Ah.

372
00:21:26,260 --> 00:21:40,340
Oh, m'lady.

373
00:21:40,340 --> 00:21:40,380
Oh, m'lady.

374
00:21:40,380 --> 00:21:41,460
Oh, m'lady.

375
00:21:41,460 --> 00:21:55,720
I... remember.

376
00:21:55,720 --> 00:22:06,640
All of it.

377
00:22:10,380 --> 00:22:12,220
Soukous...

378
00:22:13,220 --> 00:22:13,340
I don't know.

379
00:22:13,360 --> 00:22:14,860
Maybe you might...

380
00:22:18,860 --> 00:22:19,020
Yeah.

381
00:22:23,220 --> 00:22:26,000
I look.

382
00:22:30,240 --> 00:22:34,740
As we come along...

383
00:22:34,740 --> 00:23:04,720
Thank you.

384
00:23:04,740 --> 00:23:34,720
Thank you.

385
00:23:34,740 --> 00:23:36,740
Thank you.

